<Shell title="Ahimanikya Satapathy · Founder"><div class="wrap"><div class="page-head"><p class="eyebrow">Founder & Editor-in-Chief</p><h1>Ahimanikya<br/><em class="highlight">Satapathy.</em></h1><p class="lead">Rediscovering the stories of a place.<br/>Reimagining what they can make possible.</p></div><div class="prose section" style="padding-top:0"><p>Ahimanikya founded Project Odisha with an ambition to make Odisha’s people, places, culture and knowledge easier to discover—and to connect that understanding with opportunities for the state.</p><p>The project brings together research, photographs, local knowledge and stories that can be explored, questioned and enriched over time. It welcomes a connection with Odisha whether you live there, trace your roots there or are discovering it for the first time.</p><h2>A living project.</h2><p>As Founder & Editor-in-Chief, Ahimanikya shapes the direction of the project and its editorial work. His ambition is a shared resource that grows through thoughtful contributions and gives credit to the people and sources behind it.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button utk-button" href="/explore/">Explore the collection ↗</a><a class="text-link" href="/contribute/">Be part of the story →</a></div></div></div></Shell>
